IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fca4a-dates`
IMPORT `fca4a-rules`
IMPORT `fca4a-seat`

-- Federal Court of Australia Act 1976 (Cth), Part IVA -- cases for the claimant's questions (fca4a-seat.l4).
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text (Compilation No. 59, and the Federal Court Rules 2011,
-- Compilation No. 11), with the section, and never copied from the encoding's output. Day counts are worked in the
-- comments. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the claimant in a class action`

§§ `ss 33B, 33C, 33G -- can the claim be in a class action`

-- Order: day it arose, claimants (counting me), shared circumstances, substantial common issue, cross-vesting only.
-- s 33B: the 1991 Act commenced 4 March 1992 (endnotes); a cause arising that day is after commencement (fork F1).
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 4 3 1992) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 3 3 1992) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 15 3 2025) 500 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 33C(1)(a): "7 or more persons".
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 15 3 2025) 6 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33C(1)(b), (c).
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 15 3 2025) 7 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 15 3 2025) 7 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33G.
#ASSERT `Can my claim be brought in a class action?` (`the day` 15 3 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 33D -- standing`

#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 15 3 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 33D(1) is silent on a person without a sufficient interest of their own.
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 15 3 2025) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 33C fails: a no, whatever the standing.
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 15 3 2025) 6 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I start the class action as representative party?` (`the day` 1 1 1990) 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33D(2).
#ASSERT `Can I keep running the class action without a claim of my own?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I keep running the class action without a claim of my own?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 33A, 33E, 33F -- the group`

#ASSERT `Am I a group member?` TRUE `an individual or a company or other person not listed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member?` FALSE `an individual or a company or other person not listed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member?` FALSE `the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member?` TRUE `the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member?` TRUE `the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member?` TRUE `a Minister of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member?` TRUE `a public-purpose body corporate that is not an incorporated company or association` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a group member?` TRUE `an officer of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory acting as such` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I consent to be a group member?` `an individual or a company or other person not listed` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I consent to be a group member?` `the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I consent to be a group member?` `a Minister of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I consent to be a group member?` `a public-purpose body corporate that is not an incorporated company or association` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I consent to be a group member?` `an officer of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory acting as such` EQUALS TRUE
-- s 33F(1), (2); not under disability: the section is silent.
#ASSERT `Do I need a next friend or committee?` TRUE `be a group member` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I need a next friend or committee?` TRUE `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I need a next friend or committee?` FALSE `take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 33J -- opting out`

-- Opt-out date 30 June 2026. "before the date so fixed": 29 June is the last day; 30 June is too late.
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the class action?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 29 6 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the class action?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 1 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the class action?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 30 6 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the class action?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 1 7 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not in writing / Form 21: outside the grant's wording (fork F3); late and unwritten: the period answers first.
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the class action?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 29 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the class action?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33ZC(8): no opt-out from an appeal.
#ASSERT `Can I opt out of the class action?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 29 6 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `By when must I opt out?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) EQUALS `the day` 29 6 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I opt out?` (`the day` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `the day` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `By when must I opt out?` (`the day` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `the day` 31 12 2025
-- s 33J(4): "must not commence earlier than" the opt-out date; on the date itself it may.
#ASSERT `Can the hearing start before my opt-out date?` (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the hearing start before my opt-out date?` (`the day` 29 6 2026) (`the day` 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the hearing start before my opt-out date?` (`the day` 29 6 2026) (`the day` 30 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the hearing start before my opt-out date?` (`the day` 1 7 2026) (`the day` 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 33ZB -- bound by the judgment`

#ASSERT `Will the judgment bind me?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Will the judgment bind me?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will the judgment bind me?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Will the judgment bind me?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 33K -- a later claim`

-- Class action began 1 February 2026; the Court fixes 1 June 2026. "after the commencement ... but before such date".
#ASSERT `Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` (`the day` 2 2 2026) (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` (`the day` 31 5 2026) (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` (`the day` 1 6 2026) (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` (`the day` 2 2 2026) (`the day` 1 2 2026) (`the day` 1 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 33ZE -- the time limit`

-- Old last day 31 Dec 2026; class action began 1 Jul 2026. Days from 1 Jul to 31 Dec 2026: 31+31+30+31+30+30 = 183.
-- Opted out 1 Mar 2027: 1 Mar + 183 days: to 1 Sep is 31+30+31+30+31+31 = 184, so 183 days is 31 Aug 2027.
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 31 12 2026) (`the day` 1 7 2026) `I opted out` (`the day` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `my limitation period runs again` (`the day` 31 8 2027)
-- Ended without disposing of my claim on 15 Jan 2027: to 15 Jul is 31+28+31+30+31+30 = 181, plus 2: 17 Jul 2027.
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 31 12 2026) (`the day` 1 7 2026) `the class action and its appeals ended without finally disposing of my claim` (`the day` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `my limitation period runs again` (`the day` 17 7 2027)
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 31 12 2026) (`the day` 1 7 2026) `the class action is still going` (`the day` 1 1 2030) EQUALS `my limitation period is suspended`
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 31 12 2026) (`the day` 1 7 2026) `my claim was finally disposed of` (`the day` 1 1 2028) EQUALS `my claim was finally disposed of in the class action`
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` FALSE (`the day` 31 12 2026) (`the day` 1 7 2026) `I opted out` (`the day` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `section 33ZE does not reach my claim`
-- Old last day 30 Jun 2026, the day before the class action began: already run out.
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 30 6 2026) (`the day` 1 7 2026) `I opted out` (`the day` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `my limitation period had already run out when the class action began`
-- Class action began on the old last day: 0 days left; opting out on 10 Jul 2026 leaves that day only (fork F14).
#ASSERT `What happens to my time limit?` TRUE (`the day` 1 7 2026) (`the day` 1 7 2026) `I opted out` (`the day` 10 7 2026) EQUALS `my limitation period runs again` (`the day` 10 7 2026)

§§ `ss 33X, 33Y(8) -- notices`

-- Order: subject, damages claimed, dispensed, ordered, Court satisfied it is just without notice.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `the start of the class action and my right to opt out` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `the start of the class action and my right to opt out` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33X(2): the Court may dispense only where no damages are claimed.
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `the start of the class action and my right to opt out` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `the respondent's application to dismiss for want of prosecution` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `the respondent's application to dismiss for want of prosecution` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `the representative party's application to withdraw` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Dispensed but then ordered under s 33X(5).
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `the representative party's application to withdraw` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 33X(3): "If the Court so orders".
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `money paid into Court in answer to a claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `money paid into Court in answer to a claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 33X(4).
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `an application to approve a settlement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `an application to approve a settlement` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `an application to approve a settlement` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 33X(5).
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `another matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be given notice of this?` `another matter` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does missing a notice affect the class action?` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 33T, 33W -- the representative party`

#ASSERT `Can the representative party be replaced?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the representative party be replaced?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the representative party withdraw?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the representative party withdraw?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the representative party withdraw?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 33L, 33M, 33N, 33P -- stopping`

-- s 33L: "fewer than 7".
#ASSERT `Can the class action be stopped?` 6 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the class action be stopped?` 7 FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33M: both limbs.
#ASSERT `Can the class action be stopped?` 7 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the class action be stopped?` 7 FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the class action be stopped?` 7 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 33N.
#ASSERT `Can the class action be stopped?` 100 FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my own claim after the class action stops?` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I go on with my own claim after the class action stops?` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 43(1A), ss 33Q(3), 33R(2) -- costs`

#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a group member who is not a party` `costs of the proceeding generally` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a group member who is not a party` `costs of the issues common to my sub-group` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a group member who is not a party` `costs of an issue about one member's claim only` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a group member allowed to appear on an issue about my own claim` `costs of an issue about one member's claim only` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a group member allowed to appear on an issue about my own claim` `costs of the proceeding generally` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a group member allowed to appear on an issue about my own claim` `costs of the issues common to my sub-group` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a sub-group representative party who is not the representative party` `costs of the issues common to my sub-group` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a sub-group representative party who is not the representative party` `costs of the proceeding generally` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `a sub-group representative party who is not the representative party` `costs of an issue about one member's claim only` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `the representative party` `costs of the proceeding generally` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `the representative party` `costs of the issues common to my sub-group` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `the representative party` `costs of an issue about one member's claim only` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 33ZJ -- the representative's costs out of the damages`

-- Excess 500,000 - 300,000 = 200,000, under the damages.
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` TRUE TRUE 500000 300000 10000000 EQUALS JUST 200000
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` TRUE TRUE 300000 300000 10000000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` TRUE TRUE 200000 300000 10000000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` FALSE TRUE 500000 300000 10000000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` TRUE FALSE 500000 300000 10000000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Excess above the damages: no more than the damages (fork F11).
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` TRUE TRUE 500000 300000 150000 EQUALS JUST 150000
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` TRUE TRUE 500001 300000 200000 EQUALS JUST 200000
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` TRUE TRUE 500000 300000 200000 EQUALS JUST 200000
#ASSERT `How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` TRUE TRUE 499999 300000 200000 EQUALS JUST 199999

